WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.884
Cognitive Load Theory commonly separates load into useful categories.

2
00:00:03.884 --> 00:00:09.062
Intrinsic load comes from the inherent complexity of the material or task.

3
00:00:09.062 --> 00:00:13.809
Some topics have many interacting elements that must be understood together.

4
00:00:13.809 --> 00:00:21.145
Extraneous load comes from the way information is presented when that presentation makes learning harder than necessary.

5
00:00:21.145 --> 00:00:28.050
Germane processing, at a practical level, is the useful mental effort learners invest in building understanding.

6
00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:31.071
Element interactivity is central to intrinsic load.

7
00:00:31.071 --> 00:00:39.270
If a task has many parts that depend on each other, the learner has to process those relationships together.

8
00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:44.449
For example, learning a single term may be low in element interactivity.

9
00:00:44.449 --> 00:00:49.627
Learning a process where timing, roles, conditions, and exceptions interact is higher.

10
00:00:49.627 --> 00:00:58.258
Designers cannot remove all intrinsic load without changing the task, but they can manage how much complexity appears at once.

11
00:00:58.258 --> 00:01:00.847
Extraneous load is the avoidable burden.

12
00:01:00.847 --> 00:01:12.499
It appears when slides are cluttered, labels are unclear, diagrams are separated from explanations, navigation is confusing, examples are weak, or narration fights with on-screen text.

13
00:01:12.499 --> 00:01:20.698
Learners may spend effort locating information, reconciling duplicate explanations, or ignoring decorative material instead of understanding the core idea.

14
00:01:20.698 --> 00:01:25.877
That effort feels like learning work, but it does not help much.

15
00:01:25.877 --> 00:01:30.624
The practical distinction is productive mental effort versus wasted mental effort.

16
00:01:30.624 --> 00:01:35.802
Productive effort helps learners connect ideas, form schemas, and prepare for performance.

17
00:01:35.802 --> 00:01:39.254
Wasted effort is friction created by the instruction.

18
00:01:39.254 --> 00:01:45.296
Good design cannot make every topic easy, and it should not remove all challenge.

19
00:01:45.296 --> 00:01:51.769
But it can protect learner attention by reducing unnecessary difficulty and directing effort toward understanding.
